--- !u!114 &1885153197
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1885153196}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3142328ce6992ba47b93a300cc2864ac, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::NPC_Dialogue
  dialoguePanel: {fileID: 2520466111762878362}
  dialogueText: {fileID: 2520466111762878361}
  dialogue:
  - Greek statues changed a lot over time. Early statues from the Archaic Period
    stood stiff and straight. Many were created as grave markers or to honor the
    gods.
  - 'During the Classical Period, artists became interested in making people look
    more natural. '
  - Later, during the Hellenistic Period, sculptures became even more expressive,
    with carved detailed facial expressions and dramatic poses!
  - 'The Romans admired Greek sculptures so much that they created many copies, helping
    preserve artworks that would otherwise have been lost. '
  - 'Did you know? Many Greek statues were originally painted with bright colors.
    They weren''t plain white like we often imagine today! '
  contButton: {fileID: 2520466111762878360}
  wordSpeed: 0.05
